  "summary": "A reciprocating compressor squeezes gas with a piston moving in a cylinder. In this double-acting, crosshead-type machine both ends of the cylinder work: while one end draws gas in through its suction valves, the other end compresses gas and pushes it out through its discharge valves. Automatic plate valves open and close only by the pressure difference across them.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive-displacement compressor (reciprocating)",
    "type": "Horizontal, single-stage, double-acting, crosshead, lubricated"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "cylinders": 1,
    "action": "Double-acting",
    "valves": "4 automatic plate valves (2 suction, 2 discharge)",
    "drive": "Direct-coupled induction motor"
  },
